invariant: INV-74
file: src/tcp_seal.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: ch_seal_in_place takes an n whose records do not fit cap and
  seals past the end of the caller's buffer, where tcp_nonblocking.h has it
  refuse the write whole with CH_ECAP and change nothing. The loop's write
  one byte short of its two records requires the refusal.

--- old
    if (n > tls_writable_len(t, cap)) {
        return CH_ECAP;
    }
--- new
